      "heading": "What HVAC Means in a Car",
      "html": "<p>Heating, ventilation, and air conditioning are three jobs done by one connected system. Heating warms the cabin using heat the engine already made. Ventilation brings in fresh air and moves air around the cabin. Air conditioning removes heat and moisture from cabin air so it feels cool and dry.</p>\n<p>A driver notices the system only when one of those jobs fails: no heat on a cold morning, stale air, or warm air from the vents on a hot day. A technician's job is to work out which job failed and which part of the system is responsible, instead of guessing and replacing parts.</p>\n"
