      "heading": "The Refrigeration Loop in Plain Words",
      "html": "<p>The loop has five main parts in a circle: compressor, condenser, receiver-drier or accumulator, expansion device, and evaporator. The compressor squeezes low-pressure refrigerant gas into a hot, high-pressure gas. The condenser, in front of the car, lets air blow across that gas so it gives up heat and becomes a liquid.</p>\n<p>The expansion device lets that liquid spray into the evaporator at low pressure, where it boils and soaks up heat from cabin air. The cold gas returns to the compressor and the loop repeats. If any one part stops doing its job, the whole loop's temperatures and pressures shift, and the gauges tell the story.</p>\n"
