      "heading": "Why Water Drips Under the Car",
      "html": "<p>Cabin air holds moisture, and cold surfaces pull that moisture out of the air. The evaporator is the coldest surface in the system, so moisture from cabin air condenses on it, just like water beads on a cold drink on a humid day. That water drains through a tube under the car.</p>\n<p>A puddle of clear water under a car after the air conditioning has been running is normal. A technician learns to tell that harmless drain water apart from a real leak: refrigerant leaks leave no puddle, coolant is coloured and slippery, and a blocked drain backs water up into the cabin instead.</p>\n"
